diff --git a/docs/bots.md b/docs/bots.md
index 4069dc5..838153a 100644
--- a/docs/bots.md
+++ b/docs/bots.md
@@ -75,3 +75,24 @@ Bots are chat members that post messages via HTTP API. They can be members of ro
   - Bot reply goes through same `broadcast_create` + `room.receive` (unread/push/mention) as async posts.
 - Async reply: bot `POST`s raw body to `reply_to` later (existing `Rooms::BotMessagesController`, 201/422/404/401).
 - Edge: deleted room/message before job → `discard_on DeserializationError` + `rescue RecordNotFound`; webhook removed before job → `return unless webhook_url.present?`; bot removed from room before sync reply → skip post; network timeout/500/invalid URL → warn, no message, no retry.
+
+## Add to all open rooms + joined callbacks
+
+- Column `users.add_to_all_open_rooms` boolean, default false, not null — per-bot opt-in to auto-join opens.
+  - Scope `User.adding_to_all_open_rooms` (`where(add_to_all_open_rooms: true)`).
+  - Bots no longer join opens by default; humans still do.
+  - `User#grant_membership_to_open_rooms` (after_create_commit): humans bulk-insert all opens; bots only if `add_to_all_open_rooms?` via `join_all_open_rooms` (loops `Rooms::Open.find_each { |r| r.memberships.grant_to(self) }` so joined notifies).
+  - `User#grant_missing_open_rooms_if_add_to_all_enabled` (after_update_commit, `saved_change_to_add_to_all_open_rooms? && add_to_all_open_rooms?`): turning switch off→on grants missing opens; turning off keeps memberships (no revoke).
+  - `Rooms::Open#grant_access_to_all_users` (after_save_commit when `type_previously_changed?(to: "Rooms::Open")`): now `grant_to(humans)` + `grant_to(bots.active.adding_to_all_open_rooms)` — new opens + closed→open include humans always, bots only if opted in.
+- Form (`_form` shared by `/bots/new` + edit): adds switch checkbox `check_box :add_to_all_open_rooms` with label/aria-label/for-screen-reader + visible text exactly "Add to all open rooms" (QA drives by label). Styled as `.switch` with real checkbox under it (QA expects checkbox). Off by default (`User.new` gets DB default false). Permitted in `BotsController#bot_params`.
+- Joined trigger: `Room.memberships.grant_to(users)` centralizes notify — computes `new_ids = user_ids - existing_ids` before `insert_all` (which is `ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING`, skips dups), then unless `room.direct?`, `User.bots.active.with_webhook.where(id: new_ids).find_each { |bot| BotJoinedJob.perform_later(room, bot) }`. Covers closed create (`Room.create_for`), closed update (`revise`), open grant, bot switch-on (`join_all_open_rooms`), new-bot-on. Exactly once per room (dups skipped, no re-notify on re-save). `Membership#after_create_commit :notify_bot_joined` safety net for direct `create!` (insert_all bypasses callbacks, so no double).
+  - `Room::BotJoinedJob(room, bot)` with `self.enqueue_after_transaction_commit = true` (defers enqueue inside `Room.create_for`/`revise` transactions until commit), `discard_on DeserializationError`, `rescue RecordNotFound`. Skips directs, non-bots/inactive/no-webhook.
+  - `Room::BotWebhookNotifier(room:, bot:, message: nil)` extended: `notify` (mention, requires message) unchanged + `notify_joined` (checks `!direct?`, webhook+token, builds joined payload, same `post_payload` + `handle_response` as mention so sync reply identical). Initializer made `message:` optional for backward compat (`BotMentionJob` still passes `message:`).
+- Payload (`Content-Type: application/json`):
+  ```json
+  { "event": "joined", "room": {"id": 5, "name": "Ops", "reply_to": "/rooms/5/:bot_token/messages"} }
+  ```
+  - `reply_to`: `room_bot_messages_path(room.id, bot.bot_token)` — same async posting URL as mention.
+  - Directs never trigger (checked in `grant_to`, `Membership`, job, notifier).
+- Sync reply: same as mention — `200` + `text/plain`/`text/html`/blank-CT with non-blank scrubbed body → `room.messages.create!(creator: bot)` + `broadcast_create` (membership re-checked); `204`/other types/statuses ignored; network errors warned, no retry.
+- Edge: switch-on with no opens → no-op; switch-off then new open → not added; bot already member of closed converted to open → no duplicate joined (already member); remove+re-add → joined again (new landing); bot without webhook → membership but no job; webhook removed before job → skip; bot removed before reply → skip post; closed with multiple bots → one job per bot.
